  data: {
    LLM: 'Phase one: all players play one card to each trick (from hand or stock). Suits do not matter; highest rank wins. Ties are broken by tied players playing again until one wins. After playing, each player draws from the stock to keep three cards until stock is empty. When a player has no card to play, phase one ends; players combine hand and won cards for phase two. Phase two: each turn beat the previous card or sequence, or pick up the lowest (earliest) card or sequence in the trick. Last player with cards loses.',
